%% cssn_boot.glp --- CSSN's app on two smartphones (SGSG paper, Section 7):
%% under the boot harness, one isolate per person, each with its own key pair,
%% running the social graph of graph/core as its super-app and hosting CSSN's
%% mini-app, the program compiled from CSSN's contract (programs/cssn).  Each
%% person trusts the bundled compiler's key, reads the certified artefact
%% cssn.glpw from graph/core with load_file/2 and installs it, giving the
%% super-app one end of its person channel; alice cold-calls bob, they
%% befriend across the isolates, alice invites him to the app, bob consents,
%% and the handshake opens a root channel of the app's own protocol between
%% their two executions, each activated by run/3, over which the two befriend
%% in the app, as GSN's app's in superapp_boot.glp.  The program is
%% graph/core, named as :boot's second argument:
%%   :artefact programs/cssn programs/social/graph/core
%%   :boot programs/social/cssn_boot.glp programs/social/graph/core
%% Expected on the persons' screens: [alice] view(alice, [friend(bob),
%% knows(bob), identity, person], [bob], [], _), and bob's likewise.

procedure boot.
boot :-
    agent(ch(_?, _), ch(_?, _))@alice,
    say(alice, cssn_invite, [bob], ch(_?, _))@alice,
    agent(ch(_?, _), ch(_?, _))@bob,
    say(bob, cssn_consent, [alice], ch(_?, _))@bob.

%% Every agent's initial goal is agent(ch(_?,_),ch(_?,_)), the person channel
%% first and the network channel second (GLP-Spec maglp.tex, Definition
%% "Multiagent GLP"), which the program, graph/core, answers: a boot defines
%% no agent/2, and the person goal's first act names the entry the program
%% starts (IGLP 0e1c9e0, Implementation Notes, "Boot").  The person scripted
%% at each agent, say/4, run on its person channel in the person's place,
%% tells the agent the entry, sg_init/4, with its own key, its mode and the
%% keys of the peers it knows, its ground arguments, alice and bob being the
%% atoms that stand for the keys in a simulation ("An agent learns the keys of
%% its peers from its person"; Remark "Agent Names"), and reads nothing.
SayAct ::= sg_init(Key, Constant, List(Key)).
SayIn  ::= [SayAct | SayEnd].
SayEnd ::= [].

exported procedure say(Key?, Constant?, List(Key)?, Channel(Stream(Constant), SayIn)?).
say(P, M, Qs, ch(_, [sg_init(P?, M?, Qs?)])).
